 <li><strong>Total private-label launch budget: $3,500-$18,000 depending on complexity</strong>. Breakdown: mold tooling $0-5,000 (if using existing mold vs custom housing), packaging design $500-2,000, certification testing $1,500-5,000, first order deposit (30% of PO value). A "minimum viable launch" with existing ODM mold + laser logo + 500 units can start at $3,500.</li>
 <li><strong>FOB pricing at MOQ 500 for private-label power banks (Grade-A cells, factory-direct)</strong>: 5,000mAh basic ~$4.80-6.50, 10,000mAh with digital display ~$5.80-8.00, 20,000mAh 65W laptop-capable ~$12.00-16.00, semi-solid-state 10,000mAh ~$14.00-18.00. <strong>Budget factories using generic Chinese cells quote 15-25% lower</strong>, but at the cost of higher defect rates (2-5% vs <0.3%) and 3-5× higher field returns. Add $0.50-1.00/unit for custom packaging with your brand's UPC barcode and retail-ready box.</li>
 <li><strong>6 mandatory certifications before your first shipment</strong>: CE (EU), FCC (US), RoHS, UN38.3 (air freight safety), MSDS (Material Safety Data Sheet), and WEEE registration (EU). Budget $1,500-5,000 total, 4-8 weeks. Your factory should handle testing, verify by requesting the lab's contact info and calling them directly to confirm the certificate is genuine.</li>
 </ul>
