 <!-- FAQ -->
 <section id="faq" class="mb-16">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-8 text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
 <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What is the total all-in cost to launch a power bank private label?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">All-in costs (product + logo + packaging + shipping + customs + duties) range from <strong>11-18 EUR per unit at 1,000 units</strong> for a standard 10,000mAh power bank. At 500 units: 14-22 EUR, at 5,000 units: 8-14 EUR. Plus one-time costs: EU take-back system registration (~200 EUR), WEEE registration (~150 EUR), and certification testing (<strong>$1,500-5,000 USD</strong>). A minimum viable launch with existing ODM mold + laser logo + 500 units starts at <strong>$3,500</strong>. For the US market, budget FCC certification ($2,000-5,000 USD) and UL 2056 listing ($3,000-8,000 USD, 2-3 months). Total launch budget range: $3,500-18,000 depending on customization depth and certification scope.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What MOQ applies for private-label power banks with custom packaging?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>Laser engraving (logo only):</strong> MOQ 500 units, ~$0.15/unit, permanent monochrome. <strong>Silk screen printing (multi-color logo):</strong> MOQ 1,000 units, ~$0.08/unit. <strong>UV digital printing (full-color, photo-quality):</strong> MOQ 3,000 units, ~$0.25/unit. <strong>Standard packaging with your logo:</strong> MOQ 500 units, ~€0.30-0.60/unit. <strong>Custom folding carton with full brand design:</strong> MOQ 1,000 units, ~€0.80-2.00/unit. <strong>Premium gift box with magnetic closure and foil stamping:</strong> MOQ 2,000 units, ~€2.50-5.00/unit. The complete power bank unit: MOQ 500 for OEM on existing models, MOQ 1,000-3,000 for full ODM with new mold. Model mixing within the same capacity tier counts toward total MOQ.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What certifications are mandatory for selling private-label power banks in the US and EU?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>EU mandatory:</strong> CE marking, RoHS, REACH, UN38.3 (lithium battery transport safety, $4,000-7,000, 4-6 weeks), WEEE registration, and national battery take-back scheme registration. <strong>EU 2027 requirement:</strong> Battery Regulation 2023/1542 mandates a digital Battery Passport with carbon footprint declaration and recycled material documentation, start building traceability files now. <strong>US mandatory:</strong> FCC Part 15B, UN38.3. <strong>US strongly recommended:</strong> UL 2056 (power bank safety standard, $3,000-8,000, 2-3 months), required by most major retailers and increasingly mandatory for Amazon. Budget <strong>$1,500-5,000 total and 8-12 weeks</strong> for complete certification. Always verify certificates on the issuing body's public database, fake certificates are a known problem in the industry.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Which branding method should OEM brands choose, laser engraving, silk screen, or UV printing?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>Laser engraving:</strong> MOQ 100, ~$0.15/unit, permanent single-color etch, best for premium brands wanting a minimalist look. Cannot be removed or worn off. <strong>Silk screen printing:</strong> MOQ 500, ~$0.08/unit, multi-color, most cost-effective at volume, best for budget and mid-market lines, but wears over 12-18 months of heavy use. <strong>UV digital printing:</strong> MOQ 3,000, ~$0.25/unit, full-color photo-quality with gradients, best for complex brand artwork, but requires flat surfaces. For a new brand entering the market: start with laser engraving on a dark-colored housing for maximum perceived quality at minimum MOQ. Upgrade to UV printing when your volume justifies the 200-unit minimum.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How do OEM buyers verify a power bank factory is legitimate and not a trading company?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Three verification methods: (1) <strong>Request a same-day video tour</strong> of the production floor with today's date on paper, a real factory walks onto the SMT line immediately; a trading company makes excuses. (2) Check <strong>ISO 9001 certification on IAF CertSearch</strong> and verify the factory address on Google Maps satellite view, if it's an office building in a commercial district, it's not a factory. (3) <strong>Ask to speak directly with the QC engineer</strong> (not just the sales rep), trading companies have no engineers. Red flags: only accepting PayPal/Western Union, selling power banks alongside unrelated products (drones, furniture), cannot provide UN38.3 test reports, and prices significantly below market ($5 for a "20,000mAh" unit is physically impossible). <strong>Factory-direct saves 20-40% vs intermediaries</strong> and gives direct R&D and QC access.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What are my legal obligations as a power bank importer in the EU?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Under the EU Battery Directive, anyone placing battery-powered devices on the EU market is a <strong>"producer"</strong> and must: (1) register with national take-back systems in each country you sell to, (2) join a compliance scheme and submit quarterly sales/collection reports, (3) ensure WEEE marking on products and packaging, (4) provide a Declaration of Conformity and technical file (test reports, risk assessments, BOM, design drawings) on demand. <strong>Non-compliance penalties: fines up to 100,000 EUR</strong>, product delisting on Amazon, customs seizure without compensation. Registration takes 4-6 weeks, plan this BEFORE your first order. From 2027, EU Battery Regulation 2023/1542 adds mandatory Battery Passport and carbon footprint requirements. In the US: FCC compliance is mandatory; some states like California (Proposition 65) have additional labeling requirements.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How long does private label power bank production take from order to delivery?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>Product selection and supplier evaluation:</strong> 1-2 weeks. <strong>Sample ordering and testing:</strong> 1-2 weeks (3-7 days for sample production + shipping). <strong>Branding design and artwork approval:</strong> 1-2 weeks. <strong>OEM production with 4-stage QC (IQC/IPQC/FQC/OQC):</strong> 25-30 days after sample approval. <strong>Shipping:</strong> 1-4 weeks depending on mode (air freight 5-10 days, sea freight 25-35 days to EU/US). <strong>Complete timeline: 8-12 weeks</strong> for OEM on existing models, 12-16 weeks for ODM with new development. DDP (Delivered Duty Paid) shipping is recommended for first-time importers, the manufacturer handles all logistics, customs clearance, and import duties. Payment terms: 30% deposit upon order, 70% before shipment (T/T).</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How do OEM buyers start a power bank private label order?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Define your target market (EU/US/both) and retail price point, this determines capacity, certifications, and packaging tier. <strong>Step 2:</strong> Choose your power bank model from an existing OEM catalog to minimize tooling cost and lead time. <strong>Step 3:</strong> Select branding method (laser for premium, silk screen for budget) and packaging tier. <strong>Step 4:</strong> Request 3-5 production-grade samples and test actual capacity, charging speed, and build quality. <strong>Step 5:</strong> Register for EU take-back systems and WEEE BEFORE placing your order (4-6 weeks processing). <strong>Step 6:</strong> Finalize artwork, pay 30% deposit, production begins. <strong>WOWOHCOOL offers free consultation on product selection, branding, regulatory compliance, and certification with MOQ from 500 units. <a href="/contact/" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange underline">Request a no-obligation quote for your specific power bank private label project.</a></strong></p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

